From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gert Pellin <gert@pellin.be>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:06:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Show surfaces and way types of tracks

Every track is analysed in the background (CSurfaceTrk) whenever its
points change, using the active surface databases (CSurfaceDbManager).
The track's Info tab shows two stacked bars with legend (surface classes
and way types, km and %) and a collapsible list of the detailed surfaces,
or a hint how to build a database if none covers the track.

The results are derived track point data like slope, they are not saved.
They are offered as color sources "Surface*" and "Way Type*", drawn with
a fixed color per category, with a matching legend on the map and in the
Style tab. The track point tooltip names the surface and way type.

Tool -> Create Surface Database opens a tab to build databases from .osm.pbf
extracts in a worker thread and to choose the active ones. The Routino
router panel links to it. Dutch translations included.
